## Preparing for CI

In CI, all code will be checked using this script:

```bash
go install golang.org/x/tools/cmd/goimports@latest && \
if [[ -n $(goimports -local github.com/${CIRCLE_PROJECT_USERNAME}/${CIRCLE_PROJECT_REPONAME} -l .) ]];
then
  goimports -local github.com/${CIRCLE_PROJECT_USERNAME}/${CIRCLE_PROJECT_REPONAME} -d . && exit 1;
fi
```

To pass this check, run this over all edited/added Go files:

```bash
goimports -local github.com/giantswarm/search-mcp -w <path>
```

## Dependencies

- Use `go mod tidy` after changes to `go.mod` and after `go get` commands.
